summary:
A few minutes ago I posted praise for approach of being "open to all" and supporting people from diverse and underserved backgrounds, but @jackclarkSF has pointed out to me that "open to all" may mean only "young people", which concerns me.
Quoting @catherineols
@jackclarkSF @kimmaicutler @juliagalef @patrickc @SteveLohr @LauraDeming I hadn't seen that yet. @LauraDeming @patrickc can we get a statement on this? "Open to all" and "young people" are in direct and blatant conflict.

If you'd like access to GPT-2 in order to work on socially beneficial applications or extensions of it, defenses against generated content, etc., then IMHO you should contact OpenAI and actually make a request. The type of requests they get will shape their policy around sharing.
Quoting @jackclarkSF
@catherineols @jeremyphoward @soumithchintala @zacharylipton @Miles_Brundage @OpenAI Yes, we're figuring out the broader points about stuff like this. As mentioned, this and our discussion of it is an experiment, so we're gonna look at what kinds of requests we get, figure out what to do or not do, and talk about it.

